{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And one who did not lie in wait.</b> Like בצדיה (Numbers 35:20) and you are צודה my life (1 Samuel 24:12). And behold it is like the case of one who ambushes and acts intentionally." "<b>But Elohim brings it about into his hand.</b> Like for he מתאנה to me (2 Kings 5:7) — seeking pretexts and incriminations. And behold its meaning is that HaShem brought about and arranged circumstances that this one should die by that one's hand, though it did not arise in his intent. And HaShem brought this about on account of another sin that he committed, so that he would be exiled from his place. And it is written: No harm shall אאונה to the righteous (Proverbs 12:21)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {1 "Proverbs 12:21 reads לא אאונה; Ibn Ezra quotes it with לא יאונה, possibly reflecting a variant reading or a secondary corruption in the manuscript."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:36:51.846526807Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}